SPECIFICATION: Pygame Audio Effect Host
======================================

Purpose
-------
Desktop host that loads audio-effect plugins from a local folder, shows one
effect at a time with knobs and switches, loads a WAV into memory, applies the
selected effect, plays original or processed audio, and shows a playback
oscilloscope. GUI and file picking use pygame only (no tkinter).

This spec is enough to reimplement the host. Example plugins may differ; the
host must tolerate extra fields and missing optional methods.


1. Runtime and layout
---------------------
Language: Python 3.
Dependencies: pygame, numpy. No tkinter, no scipy in the host.
Entry file sits beside a plugins/ directory.

  audio_fx/
    effects.py          # host
    plugins/
      __init__.py       # optional
      volume_boost.py
      rodent_distortion.py
      ...

Run: python3 effects.py
Window: resizable, default about 980x760, dark background #121214-ish
        (18,18,20). Caption: "Effect Host". Target 60 FPS.


2. Plugin discovery
-------------------
On startup, scan plugins/ for *.py files. Skip names starting with "_".
Import each file with importlib. For every class defined in that module
(not imported from elsewhere) that has all four methods:

  get_name()
  get_knobs()
  get_switches()
  apply_effect(audio, sample_rate)

instantiate it with no arguments and append to an effects list.
If import or construction fails, print the error and continue. Do not crash.
Do not require plugins to import host types. Plugin Knob/Switch/Color classes
are duck-typed.


3. Plugin contract
------------------
3.1 get_name() -> str
    Display name for tabs and the panel title.

3.2 get_knobs() -> list of knob objects
    Each knob is treated as data. Read with getattr; never assume host methods
    such as clamp() exist on the plugin object.

    Fields (names in parentheses are aliases):
      name          str, default "Generic"
      min (min_val) float, default 0.0
      max (max_val) float, default 1.0
      default       float, default 0.5
      click_pts (clicksPts)
                    list of floats in [min, max], default []
      knob_color_scheme (knobColorScheme)
                    object with outline, face, needle
                    or a 3-list [outline, face, needle]

    Colors may be "#RGB", "#RRGGBB", a named color (black, white, red, green,
    blue, gray/grey, orange, yellow, silver), or an (r,g,b) tuple.

    Default knob scheme if missing:
      outline=black, face=white, needle=black

3.3 get_switches() -> list of switch objects
      name     str, default "Enable"
      default  bool, default True

3.4 apply_effect(audio, sample_rate) -> ndarray
    audio: float32 (or float) in roughly [-1, 1], shape (n,) or (n, channels).
    sample_rate: int Hz.
    Return an array of the same rank and length (or host will not assume
    length change; plugins should pad/trim themselves).

    Before calling apply_effect, the host copies GUI values onto the effect
    instance as attributes:
      setattr(effect, knob_name, value)
      setattr(effect, sanitized_lower_name, value)
    Same for switches (bool).
    sanitized_lower_name: lowercase, non-alnum -> "_".
    Example: "Gain" -> effect.Gain and effect.gain
             "Enable" -> effect.Enable and effect.enable

    apply_effect must not take a long parameter list for knobs. It reads
    members already written on self.

3.5 Optional get_colors() -> dict
    Called on the effect instance when building its panel and tab.
    Keys and defaults:

      face           #1e1e1e   effect panel background
      edge           #46464e   panel / button border
      text           #e6e6e6
      muted          #a0a0a8
      button         #37373e
      button_hot     #50505c
      button_on      #326e50
      button_text    #e6e6e6
      switch_on      #329650
      switch_off     #46464c
      slider         #323238
      slider_handle  #468cd4
      knob_outline   #000000   used if a knob has no scheme
      knob_face      #ffffff
      knob_needle    #000000

    Also accept attributes on the effect with those names, plus aliases:
      panel, panel_face, face_color, background -> face
      border, outline -> edge
      button_color -> button
      knob_color -> knob_face

    Missing method or key -> use the default above.
    Per-knob scheme overrides panel knob_* colors for that knob only.

3.6 Optional members
    Plugins may keep live values in __init__ (self.gain, self.enable, ...).
    Extra methods and classes in the file are ignored.


4. Color parsing
----------------
parse_color(value, default):
  None or empty -> default
  tuple/list of >=3 numbers -> (int r, int g, int b)
  "#RGB"  -> expand each hex digit
  "#RRGGBB" (ignore extra trailing chars after 6)
  else named-color table, else default

Never crash on bad color strings.


5. Main window chrome
---------------------
Top row buttons (host-styled, not plugin-colored):
  Open WAV | Render | Play Processed | Repeat | Original | Stop

Second row:
  < Prev | Next > | one tab per loaded effect

Status line under the tabs.

Keyboard when file dialog is closed:
  Left or ","  previous effect
  Right or "." next effect

Only the selected effect panel is drawn. Hidden panels keep their knob and
switch values. Render applies only the selected effect, not a chain.


6. Effect panel UI
------------------
A rounded rectangle using plugin face/edge/text.

Title: get_name() at top-left.

Knobs in a horizontal row:
  Circular face, outline ring, tick marks at click_pts, needle from center.
  Needle angle: value min maps to 225 degrees, max to -45 degrees
  (270 degree sweep, like a guitar amp).
  Label under the knob, numeric value under the label.
  Horizontal slider under that; thumb position matches the same value.
  Dragging the knob or the slider updates the same value.
  While dragging, if the value is within 3% of the min-max span of a
  click_pt, snap to that point.
  Clamp to [min, max] in the host; do not call knob.clamp().

Switches under the knobs:
  Pill toggle + label. On uses switch_on, off uses switch_off.

Tab for that effect uses the same plugin button colors.
Selected tab uses button_on.


7. WAV load and memory
----------------------
Open WAV opens an in-pygame file browser (not OS dialog, not tkinter).
Start in the host script directory; user can enter folders, go "..",
scroll wheel, pick *.wav, or Cancel / Escape.

Read with the stdlib wave module + numpy:
  8-bit unsigned -> float centered at 0
  16-bit signed / 32768
  24-bit packed / 8388608
  32-bit signed / 2147483648
Shape always (n, channels), mono as (n, 1).
Keep original buffer. Processed buffer starts unset.
Unsupported widths: show error in status, do not crash.


8. Render and playback
----------------------
Render:
  If no file, status "Open a WAV file first."
  Copy original, push GUI settings into the active effect, call
  apply_effect(copy, sample_rate), store float32 result, play it.

Play Processed and Repeat: play stored processed buffer, or prompt to
Render first.
Original: play the untouched buffer.
Stop: halt mixer; clear scope freeze capture.

Playback: pygame.mixer, stereo int16, frequency = file sample rate.
Rebuild mixer if rate changes. Convert mono to dual channel.
Clip to [-1, 1] before int16.


9. Oscilloscope
---------------
Sits under the active effect panel. Height about 240 px.
Title "Oscilloscope  1 V/cm". Buttons: Freeze (toggle), Synchronize
(toggle).

Scale:
  Digital sample ±1.0 is ±1.0 volt.
  1 V per centimeter.
  96 DPI => 37.8 pixels per cm.
  y = center - sample * 37.8
  Do not auto-normalize to peak. Quiet audio is small; loud audio is tall.
  Horizontal grid lines every 1 cm; center line is 0 V.

When to draw a trace:
  Only while pygame.mixer.get_busy() is true and a play position exists,
  OR Freeze is on and a chunk was captured during playback.
  If idle / stopped / finished: draw grid only, no waveform.
  Do not wrap the buffer from end to start (that caused a doubled sine).
  Use left channel only (not stereo average).

Play position: milliseconds since Sound.play() times sample_rate, clipped
to buffer length. When past the end, treat as not playing.

Synchronize:
  Every ~250 ms run an FFT (up to 8192 samples, Hann) on the current
  buffer. Peak bin from 40 Hz to min(4 kHz, 0.45*sr), ignore DC.
  period = round(sr / freq).
  Window length = two periods (at least that, cap 2048).
  Snap window start to a rising zero-crossing near the play position,
  searching forward at most one period. Do not wrap.

Without sync: window about sr/40 samples (min 256, max 2048 or file
length). Start at play position. If the window runs off the end, draw
only the remaining samples (no wrap).

Freeze: keep the last captured chunk; do not advance. Turning Freeze off
clears the capture.


10. File dialog (pygame)
------------------------
Modal overlay. Lists ".." then subdirs then *.wav.
Click dir to enter. Click wav to load and close.
Cancel button and Escape close without loading.


11. Robustness
--------------
Host must work if:
  plugins folder is empty
  a plugin file raises on import
  Knob has no clamp / click_pts / color scheme
  get_colors is absent
  apply_effect returns the input unchanged
  numpy or pygame missing: print install hint

Do not depend on SciPy in the host. Plugins may use it, but a failed
plugin import must not take down the app.


12. Example plugin shape (not required in the host file)
--------------------------------------------------------
class VolumeBoost:
    def __init__(self):
        self.name = "Volume Boost"
        self.gain = 1.0
        self.enable = True
    def get_name(self): return self.name
    def get_colors(self):
        return {"face": "#1e1e1e", "edge": "#222222"}
    def get_knobs(self):
        return [Knob(name="Gain", min=0.0, max=2.0, default=1.0,
                     click_pts=[0, 0.5, 1, 1.5, 2])]
    def get_switches(self):
        return [Switch(name="Enable", default=True)]
    def apply_effect(self, audio, sample_rate):
        if not self.enable:
            return audio
        return audio * float(self.gain)


13. Non-goals
-------------
No preset files, no MIDI, no real-time input monitoring, no multi-effect
rack chain, no OS-native file dialog, no tkinter.